# Dreaming runtime — local-only in EVERY install mode (trial, committed, and
# after `--graduate`). The *results* of dreaming are team content and stay
# tracked: MEMORY.md and topics/*.md. The raw inputs and the per-machine
# counter are not.
#
#   logs/    one daily note per session — each developer's own chat activity.
#   .dream/  state.json (sessions-since-dream counter, last-dream stamp) plus
#            the dream/state locks. Per-machine, meaningless to a teammate,
#            and a guaranteed merge conflict if two people commit it.
#
# A teammate pulling someone else's session logs and dream counter gets noise
# and conflicts, not signal. Nothing in here is reconstructable-from or needed
# by anyone but the machine that wrote it; the installers recreate both
# directories on demand.
#
# IMPORTANT — additive patterns only, never negations (`!pattern`).
# A .gitignore deeper in the tree outranks .git/info/exclude, so a negation
# here silently RE-INCLUDES the file and defeats a trial-mode install.
# Enforced by unit-gitignore-hygiene.sh.
logs/
.dream/
